B.bbj=new A.S("YOUR TRIBUTARY",B.m)
B.bbk=new A.S("","The Danes and the Norwegians start at war with every other realm, with war-fleets already on the coast.")
B.bbm=new A.S("The coalition:"," from turn 6, if you come close to victory, the other realms make peace among themselves and all go to war with you until you fall back. The panel at the top left says when; on Hard it comes sooner. It can turn on a runaway rival too.")
B.bbn=new A.S("AT PEACE",B.u)
B.bbo=new A.S("","Attacking or pillaging a realm you are not at war with declares war \u2014 but not while a peace still holds.")
B.bbr=new A.S("Choose who marches off.",B.u)
B.bbs=new A.S("","Then they pay 50% more tax and give more men, and your armies fight 10% harder among them.")
B.bbt=new A.S("Pillage"," a province your army stands in or borders: not your own, not one guarded by another realm's army, and only if your men outnumber its levies, who fight back.")
B.bbv=new A.S("Light raid, heavy raid or full pillage:"," the harder you strike, the more gold and the more ruin. It takes the army's whole turn, and starts a war if you were not at war.")
B.bby=new A.S("Danegeld:"," when the Danes are much stronger than you and their hosts stand at your border, they demand half your treasury (at least 100 gold) for 8 turns of peace. It only buys time: when the peace runs out, they come back. East Anglia, the land they came for, is never offered terms. Playing the Danes, you can demand Danegeld yourself.")
B.bbC=new A.S("Attacks are orders"," fought when you end the turn. Each army fights one battle a turn, and armies sent against the same province fight as one host. A realm's province with no army in it is still defended by the levies it musters.")
B.bbE=new A.S("","Playing Scotland, you start with a 6-turn truce with the Norwegians.")
B.bbI=new A.S("Recruit more troops",!1)
B.bbJ=new A.S("When turn 8 ends,"," the Danes' Great Heathen Army lands on East Anglia's coast \u2014 the kingdom they come to take (anywhere on England's east coast when you play East Anglia).")
B.bbK=new A.S("A scattered start"," (chosen when you pick your realm) gives every realm one random province with a Barracks and a small host; the rest is independent. Only the conquest goal counts, and no great Viking host lands.")
B.bbL=new A.S("Tap an army"," to select it. Green provinces are ones it can march into \u2014 your own or an ally's. Red ones marked with crossed swords can be attacked.")
B.bbM=new A.S(null,"They refuse.")
B.bbO=new A.S("Gold"," comes from taxes \u2014 the more people, the more gold \u2014 and from markets, ports and mines. Manpower comes from your people, and more from barracks.")
B.bbP=new A.S("Peace:"," a realm at war with you makes peace when it is losing \u2014 weaker than you, and none of its homeland in your hands. Peace lasts 8 turns, and neither side may attack while it holds.")
B.bbQ=new A.S("Rule 45 provinces."," Every realm wins this way.")
B.bbT=new A.S("","Your armies join only when one marches onto another, or when you press Combine.")
B.bbU=new A.S("Submission:"," a realm you have beaten \u2014 down to its last province, with part of its homeland in your hands and an army of yours at its door \u2014 offers to submit. Accept, and its land, armies and treasury join your realm.")
B.bbV=new A.S("2 moves a turn:"," march twice, or march and then attack. Marching into highland takes both moves.")
B.bbX=new A.S(null,"No active game")
B.bc_=new A.S("","Now and then an event card asks you to choose.")
B.bc1=new A.S("","The handshake button at the top right opens the realms of Britain.")
B.mg=new A.Ja(0,"left")
B.mh=new A.Ja(1,"right")
B.bc2=new A.S(B.mg,B.mh)
B.aHz=new A.rN(null,null)
B.m1=new A.dt(4,"scrollLeft")
B.m2=new A.dt(8,"scrollRight")
B.bc5=new A.S(B.m1,B.m2)
B.bc6=new A.S("Both keep the morale, veterancy and moves left.",B.u)
B.bc8=new A.S(B.m2,B.m1)
B.bc9=new A.S("Build:"," a Farm makes the population grow faster, a Market or Port brings gold, and so does a Mine where there is ore (the highlands, Cornwall, parts of Wales, the Pennines and the Mendips: +10 gold a turn); a Barracks lets you recruit there, and a Fortification makes the province hard to take.")
B.bca=new A.S(!1,!1)
B.bcb=new A.S(!1,null)
B.bcc=new A.S(!1,!0)
B.bcd=new A.S("Wales and Scotland"," can instead hold every province they started with and win 27 more.")
B.lZ=new A.dt(16,"scrollUp")
B.m_=new A.dt(32,"scrollDown")
B.bce=new A.S(B.lZ,B.m_)
B.bcf=new A.S("Walls:"," assault a fortified province (its defenders fight 30% harder per wall level), or besiege it \u2014 it falls in a few turns if your army stays beside it. Besieging a realm you are at peace with is war.")
B.bcg=new A.S("When you are attacked,"," SALLY OUT is your charge, and ABANDON gives up the province to save your men: its levies fall back to a neighbouring province you hold.")
B.bci=new A.S("","You lose if another realm wins first, or if you lose all your land and armies. The panel at the top left shows how far you have come and the rival closest to winning.")
B.bck=new A.S("","Each turn is one season, four to a year, starting in spring 793.")
B.bcl=new A.S("","Your starting provinces also build on their own, with part of your spare gold.")
B.aHA=new A.S(null,B.h)
B.bcm=new A.S(B.m_,B.lZ)
B.bcn=new A.S("Every realm can sail."," A host with ships, on the coast and not yet moved this turn, can sail to a coast within reach and march, attack or pillage there. The voyage takes its whole turn. One ship is enough, and a beaten host with ships that has nowhere to fall back to on land escapes by sea.")
B.bcq=new A.S("Only the army with ships can sail.",B.bx)
B.bct=new A.S("Leave at least one man behind.",B.M)
B.bcu=new A.S("Battles are live."," Troops and morale fall round by round. CHARGE! is a gamble: it can break a wavering enemy, but against a strong, steady line many of your men fall. Pulling back is free before the lines meet (CALL OFF) and costly after (RETREAT). A side whose morale reaches zero breaks and is cut down.")
B.bcv=new A.S("ALLIED",B.by)
B.bcw=new A.S(!0,!1)
B.bcx=new A.S(!0,!0)
B.bcy=new A.S(B.mh,B.mg)
B.bcA=new A.S("End Turn"," when your orders are given. Your attacks are fought first; then the other realms move (the map replays their moves), and you defend against their attacks.")
B.bcB=new A.S("Colonize"," a province whose people are of another culture or religion: your settlers make them your own in 5 turns, for gold (more for a crowded province).")
B.bcC=new A.S("Recruit"," in a province of yours with a Barracks. Soldiers cost gold and manpower, and each people fields its own kinds of troops.")
B.bcD=new A.S(u.X,!1)
